<title>MEXICO: Wal-Mart's Mexico unit builds in Queretaro.</title>
<headline>Wal-Mart's Mexico unit builds in Queretaro.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Wal-Mart Stores Inc's Mexican unit on Wednesday said it had begun construction of a superstore in Queretaro, the capital of the central Mexican state of Queretaro.</p>
<p>Wal-Mart earlier this month bought a majority stake in Mexican retail chain Cifra for $1.2 billion. The companies jointly operate 145 retail outlets in Mexico, including 21 Wal-Mart Supercenters and 28 Sam's Club stores.</p>
<p>((--Karina Balderas, Mexico newsroom +525 728-9562))</p>
